# Web SPA build-time config (Vite). Copy to `.env.local` for local dev. Vite inlines
# every VITE_* var into the built bundle at build time (they are NOT secrets).

# DEBT D15 — cold-start tenant default (OPTIONAL).
# If set to a valid tenant UUID, the Recon Workspace skips the "paste your tenant UUID"
# gate on first load (only when nothing is persisted yet), so a single-operator / dev
# deployment is frictionless. An explicit last-used tenant (localStorage) always
# overrides it, and the default itself is never persisted (it tracks the build).
#
# SECURITY: Vite inlines this into the shipped JS, so it is readable by anyone who loads
# the SPA. Set it ONLY for a single-tenant or dev build. Do NOT set it in a shared,
# multi-tenant production bundle — it would disclose one tenant's ID to every visitor.
# (Low severity: tenant IDs are identifiers, not credentials, and RLS is still enforced
# server-side — but don't ship it where it isn't wanted.)
# VITE_DEFAULT_TENANT_ID=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
